{"title":"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Pythagorean)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Pythagorean)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Small_Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Small Note</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Vectors)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Vectors)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(de_Gua&#39;s)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (de Gua's)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(PyTRIGorean)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (PyTRIGorean)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Heron&#39;s_Formula_Application)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Heron's Formula Application)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Pyramids)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Pyramids)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_8_(Similar_to_Solution_5)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8 (Similar to Solution 5)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular box has width <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches, length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches, and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" /> inches, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Three faces of the box meet at a corner of the box. The center points of those three faces are the vertices of a triangle with an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> square inches. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Pythagorean.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Pythagorean)\">Solution 1 (Pythagorean)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Pythagorean)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the height of the box be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>After using the Pythagorean Theorem three times, we can quickly see that the sides of the triangle are 10, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/6116ceac340b0651a5f78ae61ce11d260442e87d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2 + 64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"101\" height=\"43\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a998cc80e281848c09e80a9bd5429f9fdca258ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2 + 36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"103\" height=\"45\" />. Since the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the altitude of the triangle from the base with length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Considering the two triangles created by the altitude, we use the Pythagorean theorem twice to find the lengths of the two line segments that make up the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We find:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b0f17eb2e645b03681faeffbb66509f4868a964.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10 = \\sqrt{\\left(28+x^2/4\\right)}+x/2\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/e/72e706b3bb393d2454304ed48f18b497bd60d7fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{36}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />. Since this fraction is simplified:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d79e8d03a8b94398e1481554251db2d4f9c37f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m+n=\\boxed{041}\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Small_Note\">Small Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Small Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>The 3D version of the Pythagorean theorem can also be applied here. ~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Vectors.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Vectors)\">Solution 2 (Vectors)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Vectors)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We may use vectors. Let the height of the box be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3914c5607bf46949390af4e088bb17107565ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2h$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. Without loss of generality, let the front bottom left corner of the box be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9f36b13a11a14accae8e072c0cf34d69267bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />. Let the center point of the bottom face be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, the center of the left face be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> and the center of the front face be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9090f2e6bd5da465fea10a8c755d64e9185f61f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We are given that the area of the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/0/4b01077f46427447a997e0e351d2ed9d1d393339.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle P_1 P_2 P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, by a well known formula, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d5330790eba4f112b1838e4fdedc42bbbd022b3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}|\\vec{P_1P_2} \\text{x} \\vec{P_1P_3}|=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"150\" height=\"37\" /> \nWe quickly attain that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/a/b0a389624d7c3d9f07dc2b0907ee4d9b445b2e04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{P_1P_2}=&lt;-6,0,h&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"153\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2c32523a2c4102c660180c5fddea3fc80a645e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{P_1P_3}=&lt;0,-8,h&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"23\" /> (We can arbitrarily assign the long and short ends due to symmetry)\n</p><p>Computing the cross product, we find:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8d1f3ff90d6e84366b2191c0ed9ee6e5f4a58d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\vec{P_1P_2} x \\vec{P_1P_3}=-&lt;6h,8h,48&gt;\\]\" width=\"240\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Thus:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fe9d13192acc313b15a263061db3ba855b36026.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{(6h)^2+(8h)^2+48^2}=2*30=60\\]\" width=\"279\" height=\"32\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6ca4c0754f6eed1c850090611874530b0dc7362.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[h=3.6\\]\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c432690266a68fd4a21a2f2ed28f0b06a25c7b82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2h=7.2\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/7/cf77198c99fd6c16bded9e14dd9e5065e1c94911.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2h=36/5\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d79e8d03a8b94398e1481554251db2d4f9c37f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[m+n=\\boxed{041}\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the height of the box be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>After using the Pythagorean Theorem three times, we can quickly see that the sides of the triangle are 10, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad80f6b350406393c5595a5cc448adf65a88bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"109\" height=\"32\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/5551dc025a3be4c604ead24c2c080f74fdc64e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"109\" height=\"32\" />. Therefore, we can use Heron's formula to set up an equation for the area of the triangle.\n</p><p>The semiperimeter is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58f3a7ab046c53a7265b2e802929f5dbd21d2e12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(10 + \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 64} + \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 36}\\right)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"326\" height=\"43\" />. Therefore, when we square Heron's formula, we find\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e01d86092a1a0f7f0961c298da1fe76f913f43.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}900 &amp;= \\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\left(10 + \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 64} + \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 36}\\right)/2\\right)\\times\\left(\\left(10 + \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 64} + \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 36}\\right)/2 - 10\\right)\\\\&amp;\\qquad\\times\\left(\\left(10 + \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 64} + \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 36}\\right)/2 - \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 64}\\right)\\\\&amp;\\qquad\\times\\left(\\left(10 + \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 64} + \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 36}\\right)/2 - \\sqrt{(x/2)^2 + 36}\\right).\\end{align*}\" width=\"831\" height=\"142\" />\n</p><p>Solving, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92235c5fd83fe2b5a9cbcc5271af78fda97fb5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{041}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28de_Gua.27s.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(de_Gua's)\">Solution 4 (de Gua's)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (de Gua&#39;s)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It isn't hard to see that the triangle connecting the centers of the faces of the rectangular prism is congruent to the triangle connecting the midpoints of three edges that concur. So we can now apply de Gua's theorem (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Gua%27s_theorem\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Gua%27s_theorem</a>) to see that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/8/e88a8ffb6fde08c4e04ab73de76433d0765fea2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^2=24^2+(3x)^2+(4x)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is half the desired length of the height.\n</p><p>Solving yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/6209777b09dc54b4693a04fbb564563fae8633a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x=\\frac{36}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"64\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>And thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f644f538f51d7538138337d35ad854aad1d69ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36+5=\\boxed{041}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>---Solution 4 contributed by Siddharth Namachivayam\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28PyTRIGorean.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(PyTRIGorean)\">Solution 5 (PyTRIGorean)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (PyTRIGorean)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let half the height be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> (we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6ea4756efa52a156029529aba37a305a5cb496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />), then we see that the three sides of the triangle are (by Pyth Theorem) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/4/53441a7d8dc6f1f22a1faed7392a95c0b4097214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10, \\sqrt{a^2+36}, \\sqrt{a^2+64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" />. Using the Law of Sines with the angle as the one included between the square roots, we see that this angle's cosine is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/94063728ee323cfe7ff26fd12b3959ded8d6cf80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a^2}{\\sqrt{(a^2+36)(a^2+64)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"163\" height=\"47\" /> by the Law of Cosines, meaning that its sine is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/6/9b678cdfc6029b4a361289002c507dcd3d6ef054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{100a^2+2304}}{\\sqrt{(a^2+36)(a^2+64)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"163\" height=\"48\" />. Finally, multiply the two square-rooted sides by this sine and one-half, and equate to 30.\n</p><p>You get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95feac81baa98f2765b92f2fe062f82ed8195114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{25a^2+576} = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/a/49ab29b06c2e9cbe2a9f50cb9b93853a66fbfb44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{18}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />. However, we must find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48fa0fe30a2d43593c483709b5a7feda9ec5dc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a=\\frac{36}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"38\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92235c5fd83fe2b5a9cbcc5271af78fda97fb5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{041}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Note: You can also find the cosine of the angle formed by the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/a/e8a459dc95875ac641a22b925a5e1760b1fcb12c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a^2+64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06b3ec6ef49c43b4deb7795885a362251a1b084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{a^2+36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"21\" /> using vectors. Letting the midpoint of the height of the rectangle that we are using be the origin, it follows that the 2 sides forming the angle can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b5adfa705fc891577c236cfef19428c97ca28c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;8,0,k&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/7/1c78c4f6c24bea835b04f47aa6e2c357697f95cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&lt;0,6,k&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" />. Using the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/0023df2dd2e8d9b244dca4ffa3093400fe2cac8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\theta)=\\frac{\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}}{\\|\\mathbf{u}\\|\\|\\mathbf{v}\\|}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"137\" height=\"39\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/d/34d9effaf208f8b57912b2bde457fc700d195033.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\theta)=\\frac{a^2}{\\sqrt{(a^2+36)(a^2+64)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"239\" height=\"48\" />.</li></ul>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Heron.27s_Formula_Application.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Heron's_Formula_Application)\">Solution 6 (Heron's Formula Application)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Heron&#39;s Formula Application)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdc960c165b21ba43f7a90caa2893d40409d6944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> the height of the box. We will solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and then multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> at the end. The three side lengths of the triangle, by the Pythagorean Theorem, are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/5801998f085cf8bd35cf6871682a4efe11687edd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2+6^2},\\sqrt{x^2+8^2},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Heron's formula states that the area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff413ddf31e31144ce55970bb3ddd31ec063bc04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"186\" height=\"32\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is the semiperimeter. Applying difference of squares to make the formula less computational, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2e4c4e77b7f4cd04e3d51136262a1ceb713b05e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{(a+b+c)(a+b-c)(a-b+c)(-a+b+c)}}{4}=\\frac{\\sqrt{(a^2+b^2+2ab-c^2)(c^2-b^2-a^2+2ab)}}4=\\frac{\\sqrt{4a^2b^2-(a^2+b^2-c^2)^2}}4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"949\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbb42735e3d12a9eabaad9a606bf718c706bb2c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2+6^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e6973386e2a72e2af9a94543777a006f665669e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2+8^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. This gives us \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/a/80a9f1aa345d5f5770c020a261838fd684dc3913.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{4(x^2+6^2)(x^2+8^2)-(x^2+6^2+x^2+8^2-10^2)^2}}4=30\\]\" width=\"439\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/1/f01e4edf263cb229b209ce1cde9c9ccab9a478d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{4x^4+400x^2+4\\cdot48^2-4x^4}=120\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/2/4b27bfe7b5d3c7ef16dfc4efca6911ef56644dc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[400x^2+4\\cdot48^2=120^2\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/2/fd281298f2c097baf22fedb40923386994494599.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[25x^2+24^2=30^2\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/574430b6b162ed780c0de07d12b0a1cbdbac02cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[25x^2=6^2(5^2-4^2)\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84031eb6188237824769818a40d791b982fb5c8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[25x^2=18^2\\]\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb31cb2d65701bb1e799ae8616bc7234bdc89178.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5x=18\\]\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/5/675d0f6fc1a318b164ade62cb38f5656a3031651.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac{18}5\\]\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Now multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get that the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b73a0264209919b4a69396bdd3a01a24a9fbdc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{36}5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/c/a1c37f320e461d664863378bb6e70c1dbf3c778e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=36+5=\\boxed{041}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"187\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Pyramids.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Pyramids)\">Solution 7 (Pyramids)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Pyramids)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the rectangular prism be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/5/055dcba798b1424c44c2606d913e0f2edab1c5ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEFGH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd17cd296404d0c6d0a3c231fdb77597e9e9348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/8/a589bcb30f3b51bac61eaedc95c872c92bfbab4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e796d1b79d8777d44c0ff457e0a640adeef11fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" /> edges of the cube. It is easy to notice that the triangle given by the problem is similar to the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> by a ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e1a1a7adf986532b7598e896785a56c785f779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/5/fa5c78b0b7dd163546f4f008fb3ec23267e9c723.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BCD]=120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>We know that the volume of the triangular pyramid defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/5/8859dbfb7a9ec734e16f2a88fb5cf1104eb6a39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C,D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23e3232466e98e0fe5884d088d8e46de209f32cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot12\\cdot16\\cdot\\alpha\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}=32\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"38\" />, and we can find the volume by using the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> as the base. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, we find that the volume is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/b/9fbdfec4e75ea6e73bc5336b517e1ab790866475.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot h\\cdot120=40h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/2/382e3b69eb16ad6374b91a5910e339d6c4b75cc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h=\\frac{4}{5}\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"38\" />, and all that remains is to find an equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin of a three-dimensional plane, and let the line segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/c/72cb1a3fe84f7b1c76fc2f80bbca62064f530ad6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB,AC,AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" /> lie on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/c/accc80fdf164cef264f56a82b6f9f6add320fe05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y,z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> axes respectively. We know that the equation of the plane in which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> lies can be represented by the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/938e230852ca8b4c22862fb13059e8dd5a1bb3ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax+by+cz=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> are real values, and we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/c/d0c35b1cc3397d1286ab9717fcfadb210c73065f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(12,0,0),C(0,16,0),D(0,0,\\alpha)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"256\" height=\"20\" /> lie on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" /> which in turn lies on this plane. Thus the three points are solutions to the equation. Plugging in the values yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/2/33201882508b1f7f21a622ccd3cad4245794ba8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=12a=16b=\\alpha c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"157\" height=\"14\" />, and inserting these values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and simplifying yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9a62f1362a4c987a4c1c63a82b758c489b2aca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{12}x+\\frac{1}{16}y+\\frac{1}{\\alpha}z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"169\" height=\"38\" />. This is the equation of the plane.\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distance_formula\" title=\"Distance formula\">formula</a>, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> (or the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f372757d55c2d07adc720932c6d6e1396aa389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />) is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2f85f2ae915a634e0090066ce0adbcf51585dc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{12^2}+\\frac{1}{16^2}+\\frac{1}{\\alpha^2}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -31px\" width=\"135\" height=\"56\" />. Plugging this value in, we find that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/2/5e2fc59311a2e6d15c74afd2b03980a8143d4baf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4}{5}\\alpha=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{12^2}+\\frac{1}{16^2}+\\frac{1}{\\alpha^2}}}\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/6/006fbdcae0196e3739a6967dbb8361153d4f8a74.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{12^2}+\\frac{1}{16^2}+\\frac{1}{\\alpha^2}}=\\frac{5}{4\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f98d2b9616a9b6ada58507eabd9855d16ca12739.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{12^2+16^2}{12^2\\cdot16^2}+\\frac{1}{\\alpha^2}=\\frac{25}{16\\alpha^2}\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f42432a5847f51a5fcdadc1923b8ad688c51642.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{20^2}{192^2}=\\frac{9}{16\\alpha^2}\\]\" width=\"100\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e64b50f617494ae5c0504a82c2c765c086d7b75.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{20}{192}=\\frac{3}{4\\alpha}\\]\" width=\"76\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/9/869e320e9e5154498a55e06ac5ad898693a06174.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\alpha=\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot\\frac{192}{20}=\\frac{36}{5}\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f644f538f51d7538138337d35ad854aad1d69ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36+5=\\boxed{041}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~eevee9406\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_8_.28Similar_to_Solution_5.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8_(Similar_to_Solution_5)\">Solution 8 (Similar to Solution 5)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8 (Similar to Solution 5)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Again, consider the total height as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />, which leads to the side lengths of the triangle being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bcaa440e69267bce49f66012d6200052a5adce9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2 + 64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/a/8ba5d394520a92cb90029ab6119982a74a1ff5be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2 + 36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />. Consider the angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between the two sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9ce8a1bd988f50713495ba3a901802d0484af8cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2+36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Since the area of a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/6/fa6a0fc4be192cb2e190f5a8be5b8f41dc1974f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}ab\\sin c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" />, we can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/1/c914f12c5fce8f35e957731ba69c3777cc9076ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(10)\\sqrt{x^2+36}\\sin \\theta = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"200\" height=\"38\" />. By cosine law, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/a/5cade4941307f49e2ab71ccc3e6f390f9e0789f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+64 = x^2+36+100-2(10)\\sqrt{x^2+36}\\cos \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"369\" height=\"23\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/7/9d701d6552c0e80e9a0a018c45c878bc09e111a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20\\sqrt{x^2+36}\\cos \\theta = 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"175\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Divide the first equation by the second to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/7418244b6854da90d751852436d287a357c8b681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta} = \\frac{5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"39\" />, and solve to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b33a8812b7dcdbf84f03affb1ed4d4bce595e2f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\theta=\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{34}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"98\" height=\"43\" />. Substitute this back into the first equation to get the following:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e7f48879fa7395443d547f842ed4246ea26ae1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{x^2+36} = \\frac{6}{5}\\sqrt{34}\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c91f6f692daa85edeb1738d337d9408ea857d5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+36 = \\frac{36}{25}(34)\\]\" width=\"134\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/d/73d011c822ea65aa9f6da85b5df9521979d8af14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 = \\frac{36(34)-36(25)}{25}\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d6dbe2c1c8dfef252d78d831a90c045096fd21.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{18}{5}\\]\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a25fad0309bf247167695faec82fd9f6569cb550.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x = \\frac{36}{5}\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92235c5fd83fe2b5a9cbcc5271af78fda97fb5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{041}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~htoshiro\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I\" title=\"2013 AIME I\">2013 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2013 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2013\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2013 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017231313\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.069 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.088 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 815/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 26798/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.758      1 -total\n 59.72%    8.216      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.90%    5.215      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11844:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017231313 and revision id 287898. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}